details:
(a) the salient features of the Adopt a Heritage 2.0 Programme and its objectives with respect to heritage sites in Andhra Pradesh;
(b) the manner in which Monument Mitras/private and public entities are engaged to ensure quality upkeep and visitor experience at adopted sites in the State;
(c) whether any heritage or archaeological sites in Nellore district have been considered or proposed for adoption under the Programme and the current status thereof; and
(d) the steps being taken to improve last-mile connectivity and signage at adopted heritage sites in the State to enhance accessibility for tourists?

(a) the salient features of Pradhan Mantri Matsya Kisan Samridhi Sah Yojana (PM-MKSSY), including whether any insurance cover is available to safeguard aquaculture farmers coastal areas of Andhra Pradesh;
(b) the manner in which the scheme promotes environmentally sustainable and climate-resilient fisheries and aquaculture practices and whether any such interventions have been identified or implemented for Nellore district;
(c) whether the scheme is expected to boost domestic seafood exports from Nellore district and if so, the steps being taken to strengthen and deepen domestic markets; and
(d) the number of new employment opportunities anticipated under the scheme for Nellore district in particular and Andhra Pradesh in general?

(a) the current status of implementation of the Pradhan Mantri National Dialysis Programme (PMNDP) across the country, including the number of districts and dialysis centres covered and the number of beneficiaries who have availed free dialysis services so far;
(b) the State-wise number of new dialysis centres sanctioned/approved under the programme during the last two years, along with the criteria followed for identification of District Hospitals/Community Health Centres for setting up such centres; and
(c) the steps being taken by Government to ensure timely operationalisation of newly sanctioned dialysis centres and adequate deployment of trained technicians and machines at such centres?

(a) the total quantity of Phosphatic and Potassic (P&K) fertilizers allocated and actually supplied to Andhra Pradesh under the Nutrient Based Subsidy (NBS) Scheme during each of the last three years, fertilizer-wise;
(b) the total subsidy amount released for Andhra Pradesh under the scheme during the said period;
(c) the district-wise requirement, allocation and actual availability of subsidized P&K fertilizers (including DAP) in Andhra Pradesh, with specific reference to Nellore district, during the last two Kharif/Rabi seasons; and
(d) whether any shortage or supply gap of subsidized fertilizers, particularly DAP, has been reported from Nellore district?

(a) whether the centrally sponsored Flood Management and Border Areas Programme (FMBAP) is being considered to be continued past 2026 and its current status of implementation;
(b) the details of the works being undertaken in the State of Andhra Pradesh under its Flood Management Programme component;
(c) whether flood plain zoning has been considered for adoption or incentivization in the State under the scheme, if so, the details thereof, if not the reasons therefor; and
(d) whether any proposal has been received for flood control and anti-erosion works in flood-prone areas of Nellore district, and if so, the details thereof?

(a) the details of semiconductor and electronics manufacturing investments approved or under consideration in Andhra Pradesh, including the proposed Indichip Semiconductors SiC fabrication facility in Kurnool and clusters such as Sri City and Donakonda;
(b) whether any similar Electronics Manufacturing Services (EMS) or semiconductor ancillary investment is being planned or explored for Nellore district, given its port and industrial-corridor connectivity;
(c) the incentives or schemes available under Government’s semiconductor and electronics manufacturing programmes for such upcoming clusters; and
(d) the investment, employment and ancillary industry benefits expected to accrue to Nellore district from this growing electronics manufacturing ecosystem?

(a) details of tourism potential and key attractions of Andhra Pradesh identified by the Ministry, including its coastline, heritage and pilgrimage circuits;
(b) whether any request for Central assistance/funding under schemes such as Swadesh Darshan and PRASHAD has been received for circuits including Vijayawada–Amaravati–Suryalanka–Chirala, Visakhapatnam–Araku Valley and Gandikota–Belum Caves–Yaganti and if so, the status thereof;
(c) whether Pulicat Lake and the Nellore coastal-temple circuit have been considered for inclusion in any such scheme; and
(d) the Central assistance extended to Andhra Pradesh for tourism infrastructure during the last three years?

(a) the details of schemes/initiatives undertaken by Government to boost production and manufacturing of space technology in India;
(b) the number of beneficiaries of such schemes during the last five years, State-wise, including gender-wise (male, female, others) data for Andhra Pradesh and whether any such beneficiaries are located in or around Sriharikota (SDSC-SHAR), Nellore district;
(c) whether Government has considered any Production Linked Incentive (PLI) scheme for space technology manufacturing and if so, the details thereof and if not, the reasons therefor; and 
(d) the details of promotional activities conducted during the last five years to create awareness about such schemes?

(a) whether the Ministry is considering a Digital Product Passport-based traceability system to track seafood consignments from farm/harvest to export, and if so, the current stage of this initiative;
(b) whether use of AI-based tools is being explored to strengthen catch certification, cold-chain monitoring, and quality assurance for seafood exports; and
(c) the steps proposed to integrate such a system with existing certification frameworks to enhance the global competitiveness and market access of Indian seafood exports?

(a) the present status of port-led infrastructure development around Krishnapatnam Port to support Kris City, being developed by NICDIT Krishnapatnam Industrial City Development Limited, a joint venture of APIIC and NICDIT, in Nellore district, Andhra Pradesh;
(b) whether Government proposes to provide additional central support for port connectivity infrastructure such as roads, rail linkages and evacuation facilities at Krishnapatnam Port, given the scale of industrial investment envisaged in the region; and
(c) the export promotion measures being considered by Government, including under the Sagarmala Programme, to leverage Krishnapatnam Port for boosting port-led economic development in the region?

(a) the details regarding the implementation of the Pradhan Mantri Ayushman Bharat Health Infrastructure Mission (PM-ABHIM) in Nellore district, Andhra Pradesh, since inception; 
(b) the details of key components sanctioned and/or established under PM-ABHIM in that district, including Ayushman Arogya Mandirs (AAMs), Block Public Health Units, Integrated Public Health Laboratories and Critical Care Hospital Blocks, mandal-wise/facility-wise; 
(c) the total funds allocated, sanctioned, released and utilised under PM-ABHIM for Nellore district during the last five years, year-wise; and
(d) the details of list of ongoing health infrastructure projects under PM-ABHIM in that district, along with their physical progress and expected timelines of completion?

(a) whether Government has granted in-principle approval for the proposed greenfield Dagadarthi airport in Nellore district, Andhra Pradesh, given its strategic importance for seafood exports, manufacturing and agri-logistics in the region;
(b) current status of statutory and technical clearances required for the project and the broad stage at which the Public-Private Partnership bidding process presently stands;
(c) the manner in which the Central Government is extending support to Government of Andhra Pradesh to facilitate timely completion of remaining clearances and commencement of construction; and
(d) expected timeline by when the airport is likely to be operationalized?

(a) whether the Tunnel Management System has been operationalised nationally, including for the Rapuru Tunnel in Nellore district, Andhra Pradesh;
(b) the tunnel projects proposed, sanctioned, completed and operationalised in the last five years, State/district/year-wise, particularly in Nellore and Andhra Pradesh;
(c) the tunnels identified for rehabilitation, structural strengthening or safety upgrades, especially the Rapuru tunnel and others in Andhra Pradesh;
(d) funds allocated, sanctioned, released and utilised for tunnel construction, safety and maintenance, State-wise, including Nellore/Andhra Pradesh;
(e) the measures taken to strengthen tunnel safety nationally; and
(f) whether any safety audit has been conducted and the key findings thereof?

(a) the number of projects sanctioned and grant-in-aid released under the Pradhan Mantri Kisan SAMPADA Yojana (PMKSY) in Andhra Pradesh, particularly Nellore district, since 2022; 
(b) whether any proposals for Mega Food Parks, Integrated Cold Chain, or Agro-Processing Cluster components have been received/approved for Nellore, if so, the details and current status thereof; 
(c) the steps being taken to strengthen food processing infrastructure, cold storage and value-addition facilities for Nellore's agricultural and aqua produce; and 
(d) whether Government proposes to prioritise Nellore under the ongoing PMKSY cycle, given its agri-export potential?

(a) the progress made in implementing the Khelo Bharat Niti-2025 across States and Union-Territories and the mechanisms established to ensure effective coordination among Central Ministries, State Governments, National-Sports-Federations, educational institutions and other stakeholders;
(b) how Government is leveraging the Khelo Bharat Niti to strengthen India’s preparations for 2036 Olympic Games and the measures being taken to build a sustainable pipeline of medal-winning athletes across priority sporting disciplines; and
(c) the number of States and Union-Territories which have formulated, their sports policies in line with the vision and objectives of Khelo Bharat Niti?

(a) whether Government has introduced reforms to make passport services more accessible, efficient and citizen-centric and if so, the salient features thereof;
(b) the present status of implementation of e-Passports, including coverage achieved and the roadmap for phased expansion;
(c) whether steps have been taken to strengthen the network and service delivery of Passport Seva Kendras and Post Office Passport Seva Kendras, particularly in underserved areas; and
(d) the details of digital and technological interventions adopted to improve transparency, reduce processing time and enhance the overall passport service experience?

(a) whether the Ministry is considering exploring the potential of “Turtle Trails” along the Andhra Pradesh coastline, including nesting stretches in Nellore district and if so, the details thereof;
(b) whether the Ministry proposes to consult and collaborate with the Andhra Pradesh Forest Department, given its existing Olive Ridley turtle hatchery and conservation programmes in Nellore and other coastal districts, while designing any such Turtle Trails initiative; and 
(c) the safeguards being planned to ensure that any such eco-tourism initiative does not disturb nesting sites and hatchling survival?

(a) the progress made under the Samudrayaan Mission, including the development and testing of MATSYA 6000 manned submersible;
(b) whether harbour and shallow-water trials have been completed and if so, the details thereof;
(c) the timeline for deep-ocean demonstration and operational deployment of the submersible; and
(d) the measures taken to promote indigenous technologies for deep-sea exploration and sustainable utilisation of marine resources?

(a) whether women’s employment and livelihood needs have been factored into the Blue Economy policy framework, particularly for coastal women in Andhra Pradesh, if so, details of the specific initiatives; 
(b) whether Government proposes to develop a dedicated strategy for women fisher workers’ cooperatives under the framework, specially in Nellore, Andhra Pradesh; 
(c) steps being taken/proposed to safeguard the livelihoods of traditional fisherwomen amid transition towards deep-sea and mechanized fishing; and 
(d) number of women fisher workers’ cooperatives currently registered, and the funds allocated and disbursed to them, in Andhra Pradesh, including Nellore district, during the last three years?

(a) the current status of Phase-I development of Ramayapatnam Port in Prakasam district, Andhra Pradesh, including the physical and financial progress achieved so far;
(b) whether there has been any revision in the original project cost or timeline since its approval and if so, the reasons therefor;
(c) the status of associated connectivity infrastructure, including road and rail links, being developed to support port operations and their expected benefit to Nellore and Prakasam districts; and
(d) the expected timeline for commissioning of Phase-I and the details of further phases, planned for the port?

(a) whether Government is exploring the adoption of autonomous vessel technology and robotics-driven shipbuilding as the country's future maritime infrastructure plans and if so, the details thereof;
(b) whether any proposal has been received or is under consideration to develop a shipyard and research hub for autonomous vessels at Juvvaladinne in Nellore district, Andhra Pradesh and if so, the details thereof;
(c) whether any Central assistance, technical collaboration or clearance has been sought or extended for this project; and
(d) the expected investment, employment generation and timeline for the proposed research and development centre for autonomous vessels and robotics-driven shipbuilding at Juvvaladinne?

(a) whether Government is aware of the growing adoption of nano urea and nano urea plus technology across the country and if so, the details of a policy framework and incentive structure to encourage domestic manufacturing and farmer-level uptake of nano-fertilizers;
(b) the details of nano urea farmer field trials and awareness-campaign in districts covering Andhra Pradesh; 
(c) whether any Central financial support has been extended to nano-fertilizer and specialty chemical units set up in Andhra Pradesh in the last two years, if so, the details thereof; and
(d) whether Government proposes to expand demonstration campaigns to more districts of Andhra Pradesh?

(a) current status of implementation of National e-Vidhan Application (NeVA) across the Houses of State Legislatures and the two Houses of Parliament; 
(b) extent to which NeVA and other digital parliamentary platforms have improved the efficiency of legislative business, including reduction in paperwork, processing time and administrative expenditure; 
(c) whether any assessment has been undertaken to evaluate performance and impact of NeVA and allied digital platforms; 
(d) if so, the key findings thereof; 
(e) whether Government proposes to further strengthen these platforms, particularly with regard to accessibility, cybersecurity, interoperability and real-time coordination among stakeholders; and 
(f) if so, the details thereof?

(a) current status of implementation of the National e-Vidhan Application (NEVA) across States and Union Territories, and the number of State Legislatures that have been fully transitioned to paperless digital proceedings so far;
(b) funding and technical support being provided by the Central Government to States, particularly Andhra Pradesh, to implement NeVA;
(c) efficiency gains, if any, observed in States that have adopted NeVA, in terms of reduction in paper usage, turnaround time for processing notices/questions, and cost savings; and
(d) the roadmap and timeline set by the Central Government to achieve “One Nation One Application” coverage of NeVA across all State Legislatures?

(a) the steps taken to address waterlogging of roads, streets and low-lying areas in coastal urban towns of Andhra Pradesh, particularly Nellore;
(b) whether an assessment has been undertaken of drainage infrastructure gaps, stormwater network capacity and urban flood management systems in Nellore and other coastal towns of Andhra Pradesh and if so, the details thereof;
(c) the measures being introduced to integrate solid waste-management with drainage upkeep; and
(e) whether there is a roadmap with specific targets and funding under national urban schemes to strengthen the drainage resilience of coastal towns of Andhra Pradesh, and if so, the details thereof?

(a) the current number of formally approved, notified and operational Special Economic Zones (SEZs) in Andhra Pradesh, along with land area utilised, investment and employment generated therein;
(b) whether any SEZ has been approved/notified in Nellore district, if so, its land area and investment details;
(c) the steps being taken to fast-track statutory clearances and attract investors to this SEZ, particularly in renewable energy, electronics and agro-processing sectors;
(d) whether any Public-Private Partnership (PPP) model is being explored to accelerate core infrastructure development and industrial allotment therein; and
(e) the timeline envisaged for full operationalisation of said SEZ?

(a) the implementation framework, financial outlay and component-wise objectives of the Designing Innovative Solutions for Holistic Access to Justice (DISHA) 2.0 Scheme proposed during the period from 2026–27 to 2030–31;
(b) the targets fixed for newly introduced VIDHI-Sanjeevani component and the Centralized Digital Platform during 2026–27;
(c) the roadmap for rollout of AI-powered Nyaya Setu chatbot under the scheme; and
(d) the monitoring mechanism proposed to be adopted to assess the outcomes of DISHA 2.0 and improve last-mile access to justice?

(a) the progress made under the YUVIKA (Young Scientist Programme) during 2026, including the number of students selected and ISRO centres participating;
(b) the major hands-on training modules, outreach activities and mentorship initiatives conducted under the programme;
(c) whether Government proposes to further expand the programme through additional ISRO centres, institutional partnerships and increased student intake and if so, the details thereof; and
(d) the measures taken to encourage participation of students from rural, remote and aspirational districts in the programme?

(a) the number and value of development partnership projects approved during the last one year through grants and Lines of Credit;
(b) the sectors covered under those projects;
(c) the progress made in introducing digital monitoring and outcome assessment of overseas development projects; and
(d) the proposed focus areas for India's development cooperation programme during 2026–27?

(a) the total amount of grants released by 15th Finance Commission to States, including Andhra Pradesh, so far and the amount pending release, State-wise;
(b) whether Government propose any mechanism to allow reallocation of tied grants as untied grants where sanitation and drinking water saturation has already been achieved and if so, the details thereof;
(c) the status of Gram Panchayat Development Plan uploads and eGramSwaraj-PFMS linked fund transfers in Andhra Pradesh vis-à-vis the national average; and
(d) whether Government proposes to publish an annual "State of Devolution Report" to measure progress across States and the timeline thereof?

(a) whether Government has undertaken any specific measures/schemes to improve income security and livelihood sustainability of shrimp farmers in the country, particularly small-and-marginal aquaculture farmers;
(b) if so, the details thereof including financial assistance provided during the last three years, year-wise and State-wise;
(c) whether Government has assessed the impact of high input costs, disease outbreaks (including white spot disease and other viral infections) and market price volatility on shrimp farmers and if so, findings thereof; and
(d) whether any insurance coverage, credit-linked subsidy or risk mitigation mechanism has been extended for shrimp farmers and if so, details thereof?

(a) the funds sanctioned and released, under the Port Connectivity pillar of Sagarmala for ports currently under construction across the country, State-wise;
(b) the details of the present status and the expected date of completion of Ramayapatnam Port and Kakinada SEZ Port, including rail and road connectivity works;
(c) the details of any progress made in dredging and berth construction at these two ports; and
(d) whether any timeline has been fixed for extending Green Tug?
SR

(a) whether Government has taken cognizance of increasing cases of fake/illegal loan apps and digital-lending frauds, specially in rural-areas;
(b) if so, the details regarding number of complaints received and cases registered against fake loan apps during the last five years, year-wise and State-wise, particularly in Nellore-district;
(c) the details regarding the number of loan apps/websites blocked or taken down during the last five years and total amount of money defrauded, recovered and steps taken to provide relief to victims; and
(d) whether Government has undertaken awareness campaigns to curb fake-loan apps in rural areas, if so, the details thereof?

(a) details of MSME parks/industrial estates sanctioned and under development in the State of Andhra Pradesh, including location and implementing agency, district-wise;
(b) details of the total project cost along with the funds sanctioned, released and utilised for development of MSME parks in the State of Andhra Pradesh during the last five years, year-wise and part-wise;
(c) details of the present physical and financial progress of these parks and the expected timeline for completion of ongoing projects; and
(d) details of total number of MSME units established and employment generated in these parks so far, park-wise?

(a) the key features of Jal Jeevan Mission (JJM) 2.0 and the major changes that have been made in it as compared to the previous phase of the Mission;
(b) the implementation framework and funding pattern under the Mission;
(c) the reforms proposed to strengthen source sustainability, operation and maintenance of rural water supply systems and community participation;
(d) the State-wise funds allocated and released under JJM 2.0 during the year 2026-27; and
(e) the timeline and targets for achieving universal and sustainable rural household tap water supply under the Mission?

(a) whether Government proposes to establish uniform standards and integrated legal framework for e-notarisation platforms nationwide, following court acceptance of digital notarisation and if so, the details thereof;
(b) the details of any consultations or expert committees formed to assess security, authenticity and interoperability of e-notarised documents across States and courts;
(c) the timeline and roadmap for amending existing laws and rules to legally recognise e-notarisation in all the jurisdictions; and
(d) the measures envisaged for public awareness, training and safeguards against misuse or forgery in digital notarisation processes?

(a) the number of mobile towers established during the last five years to improve telecom connectivity in rural and remote areas, State-wise;
(b) the measures undertaken to enhance mobile and broadband connectivity in rural areas, particularly in backward and aspirational districts of Andhra Pradesh;
(c) the steps taken to strengthen mobile connectivity and network resilience in disaster-prone and vulnerable regions to ensure uninterrupted communication during emergencies; and
(d) the scheme-wise and year-wise details of funds allocated, sanctioned, released and utilised for expansion and upgradation of rural mobile connectivity infrastructure during the last five years?
P

(a) whether the Ministry/NHAI has taken note of the rising road accidents caused by stray buffaloes and cattle on National Highways, particularly in Andhra Pradesh;
(b) the number of accidents, fatalities and injuries reported during the last three years due to cattle-related collisions on National Highways;
(c) whether guidelines/SOPs have been issued for preventing cattle movement, including fencing, barriers, underpasses/overpasses and coordination with local bodies;
(d) steps taken for regular patrolling and warning signage in cattle-prone accident zones; and
(e) whether a coordinated initiative with State Governments is proposed to prevent such accidents and the details thereof?
bpn

(a) whether Government has introduced financial literacy education in schools under NEP, 2020, including budgeting, savings, credit, insurance, digital payments and cyber safety;
(b) if so, the classes/grades covered and the details of implementing agency;
(c) the number of schools and students covered during the last three years, State-wise/UT-wise; and
(d) the steps taken to train teachers and monitor learning outcomes to prevent financial fraud and promote responsible financial behaviour among students?

(a) the details of the implementation status of the Entrepreneurship Skill Development Programme (ESDP) across the country and the outcomes achieved thereunder;
(b) details of the number of training programmes conducted and candidates trained under ESDP during the last five years, year-wise, trade-wise, State-wise and district-wise, with specific details for the State of Andhra Pradesh and Nellore district;
(c) the details of the number of beneficiaries who have started enterprises or gained employment after completion of training under the programme, State/UT-wise; and
(d) the details of the funds allocated, released and utilised under ESDP during the last five years, year-wise and State-wise?

(a) whether Government has taken cognizance of the problem of groundwater contamination and salinity/seawater intrusion in coastal areas across the country, if so, the details thereof;
(b) the details of coastal districts identified as affected by groundwater contamination, including salinity intrusion, heavy metals and chemical pollutants, State-wise, as per the latest available data; and
(c) whether any assessments, surveys or scientific studies have been conducted by the Central Ground Water Board or any other agency to determine the extent, causes and trends of groundwater contamination in coastal regions, if so, the details thereof along with the key findings and recommendations?

(a) the present physical and financial progress of the rail line from Ramayapatnam port to Tettu station under the Gati Shakti Multi-Modal Cargo Terminal Policy;
(b) the approved timelines for completion of the project and whether any delays have been reported;
(c) if so, the reasons for delay and the revised timelines; and
(d) whether the Ministry has reviewed the need for direct, dedicated freight corridors to ensure seamless evacuation from Ramayapatnam Port?

(a) whether timeline has been fixed for fund release and commencement of works for the seven universities approved under PM USHA in Andhra Pradesh and the current status of each;
(b) whether a monitoring mechanism exists to ensure Universities, including Vikrama Simhapuri University, Nellore and Sri Padmavathi Mahila Visvavidyalayam, implement NEP-2020–aligned multidisciplinary reforms;
(c) whether additional PM USHA funds are proposed for Andhra Pradesh to address infrastructure gaps, especially in underserved districts; and
(d) whether guidelines based on the national workshop outcome report have been issued and how they are being implemented by State Universities in Andhra Pradesh?

(a) the number of Primary Agricultural Credit Societies (PACS) that have successfully migrated to the common Enterprise Resource Planning (ERP)-based national software as of March, 2026;
(b) the measures taken to provide broadband connectivity and hardware (biometric devices, printers) to PACS in remote and hilly areas to ensure that the digital divide is bridged;
(c) whether the National Cooperative Database (NCD) is now fully integrated with State-level Registrar of Cooperative Societies (RCS) portals through the newly released ‘Push APIs’ to ensure real-time data synchronization; and
(d) if so, the details of the integration thereof?

(a) the details of renewable energy projects sanctioned, under construction and operational in the country during the last five years, source-wise and State-wise;
(b) the details of the total renewable energy capacity added during the last five years, year-wise, source-wise and State-wise;
(c) the details of the investment made and the funds sanctioned, released and utilised for renewable energy projects during the last five years, year-wise and State-wise; and
(d) whether Government has set any renewable energy targets, if so, the details of targets along with the steps taken by Government to achieve them including strengthening grid integration and storage infrastructure?

(a) whether Government has undertaken any initiatives for the use of Artificial Intelligence (AI) in cancer screening and early detection;
(b) if so, the details of pilot projects, programmes using AI for screening of cancers along with the outcomes including accuracy of detection;
(c) the details of hospitals and technology partners involved in development and deployment of AI-based cancer screening tools;
(d) the details of funds allocated, sanctioned and utilised for the same during the last five years, year-wise; and
(e) whether Government has taken any steps to expand AI-enabled cancer screening in public health facilities, especially in rural and underserved areas?
J

(a) the total number of Income Tax Returns filed during the last five assessment years;
(b) the growth in direct tax collections during the same period under the Income Tax Department;
(c) whether Government has identified sectors with significant tax evasion risks if so, the details thereof;
(d) the number of cases detected through data analytics-based tax scrutiny; and
(e) whether the Ministry proposes additional reforms to widen the direct tax base, if so, the details thereof?

(a) the total value of India's chemical exports during the last five years;
(b) whether Government has identified major markets for expansion of exports of specialty chemicals, if so, the details thereof;
(c) the standardization measures taken to ensure global quality standards for chemical exports; and
(d) whether the Ministry has conducted trade negotiations to address regulatory barriers affecting Indian chemical exports, if so, the details thereof?

(a) whether the Ministry has integrated AYUSH facilities with the national digital health ecosystem under Ayushman Bharat Digital Mission, if so, the details thereof;
(b) the number of AYUSH practitioners registered on digital health platforms and issuing digital health records;
(c) whether telemedicine services based on AYUSH systems have been operationalised in rural and remote areas, if so, the details thereof;
(d) whether the Ministry proposes to develop AI-based tools for AYUSH diagnosis, drug standardisation or treatment protocols, if so, the details thereof; and
(e) the steps taken to create a national digital repository of classical AYUSH formulations and therapies?
bpn

(a) whether any central incentives, clearances or approvals have been granted for the newly proposed aerospace and defence manufacturing clusters announced by the Government of Andhra Pradesh in mid-2025;
(b) if so, the details thereof, including the nature of incentives, number of firms approved, investment committed and expected timelines for commencement;
(c) if not, whether Government proposes to include Andhra Pradesh under any forthcoming national scheme or policy framework for aerospace and defence manufacturing;
(d) the criteria adopted by the Central Government for extending cluster-based incentives to States; and
(e) how the proposals submitted by Andhra Pradesh stands as compare with these criteria?

(a) the key indicators currently included in the National Indicator Framework (NIF) for monitoring India’s progress towards Sustainable Development Goals;
(b) the frequency by which Government update the State Indicator Framework (SIF) to reflect the unique development priorities of different States;
(c) whether Government has successfully integrated data from the Periodic Labour Force Survey (PLFS) into the annual SDG progress reports;
(d) if so, the details thereof;
(e) when was the last SDG National Indicator Framework Progress Report released and the major highlights regarding poverty alleviation and gender equality; and
(f) details of the collaboration between MoSPI and international agencies to ensure India’s SDG reporting remains globally comparable and transparent?

(a) specific financial incentives, such as interest subvention rates, provided to micro and small enterprises under the Assistance in Deploying Energy Efficient Technologies in Industries and Establishments (ADEETIE) scheme launched in July 2025;
(b) the number of industrial sectors and clusters currently covered under the ADEETIE scheme for energy efficiency handholding;
(c) whether all 36 States including Bihar and Union Territories have successfully transitioned to issuing electricity bills in regional languages with simplified formats;
(d) if so, the details thereof; and
(e) details of methodology and industry sectors currently notified under Carbon Credit Trading Scheme launched in 2023?

(a) the implementation progress of the PM-eBus Sewa–PSM Scheme, including the State-wise allocation of e-buses under the Gross Cost Contract (GCC) model;
(b) the payment security framework established under the Scheme, including the role of Convergence Energy Services Limited (CESL) as the implementing agency;
(c) the timelines fixed for deployment and operationalisation of the sanctioned buses and the duration of operational support provided under the Scheme;
(d) whether Government has reviewed the operationalisation of the Direct Debit Mandate mechanism with the Reserve Bank of India (RBI) for recovery of dues in case of default by PTAs; and
(e) if so, the details thereof?

(a) the percentage of women among the beneficiaries who have received loans under the PM SVANidhi scheme since its inception;
(b) the number of beneficiaries who have successfully completed all stages under the PM SVANidhi scheme and availed the third loan of ?50,000;
(c) whether Government has constructed housing units in various cities under the ‘Light House Projects’ (LHPs) for the urban poor;
(d) if so, the details thereof; and
(e) the estimated cost and the timeline for the completion of the identified Light House Projects across the country?

(a) the initiatives taken by Government to curb fake news in the country;
(b) the platforms found to be involved in the spread of fake news;
(c) whether any steps have been taken to regulate or control the spread of fake news on such platforms; and
(d) if so, the details thereof and if not, the reasons therefor?

(a) whether it is a fact that Government proposes to provide drone technology to 15,000 women Self-Help Groups (SHGs);
(b) if so, the number of women SHGs selected or benefitted so far under the scheme, State-wise; and
(c) the details of funds allocated and released for this initiative?

(a) the number of contaminated sites identified, determined and remediated in the country, particularly in Andhra Pradesh under the Environment Protection (Management of Contaminated Sites) Rules, 2025;
(b) the number of such sites for which preliminary and detailed assessments have been completed so far;
(c) the number of sites where remediation plans have been prepared, approved and implemented;
(d) the funds sanctioned and utilised for these activities; and
(e) the steps taken to address orphan sites and enhance coordination between local bodies and the Pollution Control Board for speedy implementation?

(a) whether Government has taken steps to promote and preserve Indian folk arts and traditional crafts;
(b) the schemes currently supporting artisans and cultural practitioners; and
(c) whether the Ministry proposes new initiatives to safeguard fading art forms and transmit them to younger generations?

(a) current status of the PM E-Drive scheme in terms of achieving the target of 25 lakh electric two-wheelers and deployment of over 14,000 electric buses by March, 2026; 
